{
  "id": "nhs-6-min-warm-up",
  "title": "6-minute warm-up",
  "creator": "NHS",
  "description": "The NHS general warm-up used before all its 10-minute workouts: three minutes of marching, then heel digs, knee lifts, shoulder rolls and knee bends. It is timed rather than rep-based (60 heel digs in 60 seconds) and should take at least six minutes. Use it before any of the nhs-10-min workouts or a run.",
  "source": {
    "title": "How to warm up before exercising",
